    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0264" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg998"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Butler to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm this legation’s
                    cablegrams of the 20th and of even date in regard to the extradition of the Rowe
                    brothers.</p>
                <p>The latter telegram was sent upon my ascertaining, through a third party, but
                    authoritatively, that it was the intention of the Mexican Government to refuse
                    the surrender of Chester W. Rowe for extradition to the Limited States.</p>
                <p>Inclosing copies of my two notes, of 23d and 25th instants, to Minister Mariscal,
                    I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. C. Butler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




